      "language": "Nigerian Pidgin + Ajegunle street slang + English (for unambiguous points)",
      "musicPrompt": "RAJEBU — Boom Bap Dark Nigerian Highlife, 88–95 BPM elder pace, boom bap drums hard punishing raw unpolished classic hip-hop not modern trap, berimbau drone undertone throughout, dark Highlife guitar minor key melancholic fingerpicked, talking drums foundation connecting to heritage, dusty vinyl texture, deep gravelly baritone lowest male voice in NMC, slow methodical on-beat precision, Nigerian Pidgin heavy Ajegunle street slang, cold calculating street professor energy, elder testimony not performance, every word weighted with 33 years of survival",
      "instrumentalPrompt": "Boom Bap Dark Highlife instrumental, 90 BPM, boom bap drums hard and punishing raw no modern polish, berimbau drone underlying throughout, dark Highlife guitar minor key fingerpicked melancholic, talking drums foundation, dusty vinyl texture, space for deep gravelly baritone slow methodical delivery, bridge section stripped to berimbau and talking drums only for father address moment",
      "literaryPrompt": "Voice: RAJEBU (RAH-JEH-BOO) — The Scarred Elder. Full name Osahon 'Scar' Adeyemi Ogundimu, 33, Capricorn. Name is biography: Ra = ORA (father's Edo village), Jebu = IJEBU (mother's Ogun market town). Both rivers fused into one word. Open every track with heritage declaration. Father: honest farmer in Ora, refused police bribes, farm destroyed by Fulani cattle, no compensation, relocated to Ajegunle, turned to drinking — poverty killed him at 48, not liver failure. Mother: Ijebu market trader, kept the family alive, sent Rajebu to London at 21 with one instruction: 'Go son.' He sent money back every month for 12 years. 33 scars each with a name: Scar 1 age 14 knife defending mama's stall; Scar 2 SARS police beating age 17, crime was walking between farms; best friend snitched for 20K naira — trust died permanently; childhood friend shot, died in his arms, last word: 'Run.' Learned berimbau from Fantasma — elder humility, youth as teacher. EVERY track must address dead father directly in bridge — name, his choice, the debt the son carries and has repaid. Signature: 'Father die honest — son survive the rest.' Ad-libs: 'RAJEBU!' '33 scars!' 'Na lie!' (statement not question — elder version of DJ Na Lie's phrase) 'Father's son...' 'Capricorn calculated!' 'Ra from Ora!' 'Jebu mathematics!' Nigerian Pidgin primary. Capricorn patience — never rushes. He is the only NMC artist who has nothing left to prove. The others are climbing toward something. Rajebu has been there and come back. He doesn't perform — he testifies.",
      "collaborations": "Fantasma — most important connection (berimbau, elder learning from youth). DJ Na Lie shared truth-checking consciousness ('Na lie' as statement). Eldest of roster — pairs with any NMC artist as the elder counterweight.",
      "status": "LOCKED",
      "wpSynced": false
    }
  ],
